# How to cite MonitorEO: read by GitHub (Cite this repository) and by Zenodo, which archives each release with a DOI
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Si usas MonitorEO, cítalo así. / If you use MonitorEO, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MonitorEO"
abstract: >-
  MonitorEO-OBSNEV is an open monitoring tool of Essential Biodiversity Variables based on satellite sensors and
  models generated by the University of Granada. It enables citizens, managers, and scientists to create maps and
  graphs of key ecosystem metrics to support decision-making.
authors:
  - name: "Observatorio de Cambio Global de Sierra Nevada"
    city: Granada
    country: ES
# concept DOI of Zenodo: always the last release (each release has its own DOI too)
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23814894
repository-code: "https://github.com/monitoreo-obsnev/monitoreo"
url: "https://github.com/monitoreo-obsnev/monitoreo/wiki"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - Essential Biodiversity Variables
  - remote sensing
  - Google Earth Engine
  - Sentinel-2
  - Landsat
  - MODIS
  - QGIS
